// Portable libc FFI bindings (rolling).
//
// Goal:
// - Avoid duplicating `@cfg` + `@ffi.link`/`@ffi.dll` boilerplate in application code.
// - Keep the platform-specific library attachment at the boundary (the stdlib module),
//   while call sites remain platform-neutral: `import libc "std:ffi/libc"`.
//
// Notes:
// - On Linux, attaching a link dependency is required so the native backend emits a dynamic ELF and
//   enables the `dlsym` resolver for `ffi`.
// - On Windows, the native backend resolves `ffi` symbols lazily via LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress.
// - On macOS, many libc-like symbols are provided by libSystem and can be used without explicit linking.
//
// Exposed surface (v0):
// - `puts(s)`  -> i32 (sign-extended to i64 by @ffi.ret("i32"))
// - `strlen(s)` -> i64 (size_t; 64-bit on Tier‑1)

@cfg(os="windows")
@ffi.dll("msvcrt.dll")
ffi { @ffi.ret("i32") puts, strlen }

@cfg(os="linux")
@ffi.link("libc.so.6")
ffi { @ffi.ret("i32") puts, strlen }

@cfg(os="macos")
ffi { @ffi.ret("i32") puts, strlen }

